{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your mobile data issues and optimize your internet speed. First, I need to identify your account to check your line and plan details. Could you please provide your phone number, customer ID, or your full name and date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. I have identified your account. To help you get the best possible mobile data speed, I’ll guide you through a few steps. First, please turn Airplane Mode ON and then OFF on your phone. This can help reset your network connection. Let me know once you’ve done this, and we’ll continue to the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Great, thank you for doing that. Next, let's make sure your phone is set to use the fastest available network. Please set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred' on your phone. This will allow your device to connect to the highest speed networks available. Let me know once you’ve done this, and we’ll check if your data speed improves."
}

{
  "message": "That's excellent! With your phone set to 4G/5G preferred and showing excellent signal strength and 5G, you should now be getting the best possible internet speed available in your area. If you still experience slow speeds, try restarting your phone to refresh all connections. If you continue to have issues, let me know and we can run a speed test or check for any other possible causes. Please test your internet now and let me know if the speed has improved."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear your internet speed is now excellent and you're satisfied with the result! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day and enjoy your fast connection!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your service issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Your line (555-123-2002) is currently suspended, which is why you are seeing 'No Service.' The suspension is due to an overdue bill. I have just sent you a payment request for the overdue amount. Please check your payment requests and follow the instructions to complete the payment. Once the bill is paid, I can help you restore your service."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for completing the payment. Your overdue bill is now paid, and I have restored your service for line 555-123-2002. Please reboot your phone to regain service. If you continue to experience issues after rebooting, let me know and I can assist further."
}

{
  "message": "If your status bar is showing Airplane Mode, your phone will not be able to connect to the network. Please turn off Airplane Mode on your device. Once Airplane Mode is off, wait a few moments to see if your phone regains signal. Let me know if you still do not see any signal after turning off Airplane Mode."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Since you are still seeing 'No Signal' and data is disabled, let's try reseating your SIM card. Please remove your SIM card from your phone, wait a few seconds, and then reinsert it. After that, check if your phone regains signal. Let me know if you need instructions on how to do this or if the issue persists after reseating the SIM card."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying to reseat your SIM card. Since you are still seeing 'No Signal' and data is disabled, let's check your SIM card status to see if there are any issues. Please check your SIM card status in your phone's settings and let me know if it shows as 'Active,' 'Missing,' or 'Locked.' This will help us determine the next steps."
}

{
  "message": "Since your SIM card is active and working, the next step is to check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings. Incorrect APN settings can prevent your phone from connecting to the network. Please check your APN settings and let me know if anything looks incorrect or if you need instructions on how to reset them."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please reset your APN settings to the default values. After resetting, you will need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Let me know once you have completed these steps or if you need guidance on how to reset your APN settings."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your service is fully restored and everything is working again! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your MMS (picture messaging) issue. First, I’ll need to identify your account to provide the best support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name and date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help fix your MMS issue, I’ll need to guide you through a few quick checks and steps on your phone. First, can you confirm if you’re able to send and receive regular text messages (SMS) and if your mobile data is working for browsing the internet?"
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please try sending a regular text message (SMS) to see if that works. To check if your internet is working, try opening a web browser on your phone and visiting any website (for example, www.google.com). Let me know if the page loads successfully or if you see any error messages. This will help us determine if your mobile data connection is working properly."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. If your internet isn’t loading and you can’t find the Messages app, it’s possible there’s a mobile data or app issue. Let’s start by checking your phone’s status bar for important indicators. Please look at the top of your phone’s screen and let me know if you see any of these icons: an airplane (✈️), a signal strength indicator (bars), or a mobile data icon (like 5G, 4G, LTE). Also, let me know if you see any unusual icons or warnings. This will help us understand your phone’s current connection status."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for describing the icons. Since you have signal bars and 5G showing, your phone appears to have cellular service. However, since your internet isn’t loading, there may be an issue with your phone’s network settings. Let’s try resetting your phone’s APN (Access Point Name) settings, which can often fix problems with mobile data and MMS. Please follow the instructions on your phone to reset your APN settings. Once you’ve done that, let me know, and I’ll guide you through the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Yes, please restart your phone now to apply the new APN settings. Restarting your phone will not delete any of your photos, messages, or other personal data. Once your phone has restarted, let me know so we can check if your MMS and mobile data are working."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Let’s try another step that can help with MMS issues. Sometimes, the messaging app needs special permission to send picture messages. Please grant SMS permission to your messaging app. Once you’ve done that, try sending a picture message again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying those steps. Another possible cause for MMS issues is if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled, as it can sometimes interfere with sending picture messages. Please turn off Wi-Fi Calling on your phone. Once you’ve done that, try sending a picture message again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you troubleshoot your mobile data issues. First, I need to verify your account to access your line details. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Your mobile data is not working or is very slow because you have exceeded your monthly data limit of 15GB on your Premium Plan. You have used 15.1GB so far this cycle, which means your data connectivity is either cut off or severely restricted.\n\nTo restore excellent internet speed, you can refuel your data. You can add up to 2GB of extra data at $2.00 per GB. Would you like to add 1GB or 2GB of data to your line? Please let me know your preference so I can proceed."
}

{
  "message": "2GB of extra data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. You should now have restored mobile data connectivity and improved speed. If you still experience slow speeds, please let me know so I can help you further troubleshoot your device settings."
}

{
  "message": "To help improve your mobile data speed from 'good' to 'excellent,' let's check if any data-saving features are limiting your speed. Please turn off Data Saver mode on your phone by using the toggle_data_saver_mode() function. Let me know once you've done this, and we can check your speed again."
}

{
  "message": "That's fantastic news! I'm glad your internet speed is now excellent and everything is working as you need. If you have any more questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I'd be happy to help you with your MMS issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help diagnose your MMS issue, could you please check if you can send regular text messages (SMS) and if your mobile data is working for browsing the web or using apps? This will help determine if the problem is specific to MMS or related to your overall service or data connection."
}

{
  "message": "Great question! The easiest way to check if your mobile data is working is to turn off Wi-Fi on your phone and then try browsing a website or using an app that requires internet access (like email or social media). If the website or app loads, your mobile data is working. Please let me know what you find, or if you need step-by-step instructions for this process."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. Since your mobile data isn't working, let's start troubleshooting your cellular service and data connection. First, could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know if you see any signal bars, airplane mode icon, or any other unusual icons at the top of your screen? This will help determine if your phone is connected to the cellular network."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the details. Since you have good signal and 5G is showing, let's check if there are any restrictions or settings affecting your mobile data. Could you please check if Data Saver mode is enabled on your phone? This feature can sometimes restrict data usage and affect MMS. Let me know if you need instructions on how to check this."
}

{
  "message": "Thanks for confirming that Data Saver mode is off. Next, let's check if your phone's Access Point Name (APN) settings are correct, as incorrect APN settings can prevent mobile data and MMS from working. Could you please check your APN settings and let me know if anything looks unusual or if you're unsure what the settings should be?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your APN settings. To ensure everything is set up correctly, let's reset your APN settings to the default values. After resetting, you'll need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Please go ahead and reset your APN settings now, and let me know once that's done so I can guide you through the next step."
}

{
  "message": "Great! Now that you've reset your APN settings and rebooted your phone, please try sending an MMS message again. Let me know if it goes through successfully or if you're still experiencing issues."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Let's check if your messaging app has the necessary permissions to send and receive MMS, especially access to storage. Please grant storage permission to your messaging app. Once you've done that, try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for granting the storage permission. Next, let's check if your messaging app has SMS permission as well, since this is required for sending MMS. Please grant SMS permission to your messaging app, then try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "It looks like you've used up your monthly data allowance for your plan, which is why MMS messages aren't going through—MMS requires mobile data to work. You can add more data to your line (up to 2GB) for a small fee per GB, or you can consider changing to a plan with a higher data limit. Would you like to add more data to your line so you can send MMS messages right away? If so, how much data would you like to add (up to 2GB)?"
}

{
  "message": "2GB of data has been successfully added to your line for a $4.00 charge. You should now be able to use mobile data and send MMS messages again. Please try sending an MMS message now. If it still doesn't work, try restarting your phone once more. Let me know if you have any further issues!"
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are working again! It was my pleasure to assist you, and thank you for your patience throughout the troubleshooting process. If you have any more questions or need help in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your identity to access your account and provide support. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I need to check a few things on your device. First, can you please check if your messaging app has permission to send SMS messages? Please grant SMS permission to your messaging app if it is not already enabled. Let me know once this is done, or if you need instructions on how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Please grant SMS permission to your messaging app. On most phones, you can do this by going to Settings > Apps > Messaging > Permissions, then enable SMS. Once you have granted the SMS permission, let me know so I can continue troubleshooting your MMS issue."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for granting SMS permission. Next, I need to check if your messaging app can now send MMS messages. Please try sending an MMS message again. If it still does not work, let me know so I can guide you through additional troubleshooting steps."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. The next step is to check your phone's mobile data connection, as MMS requires mobile data to be enabled. Could you please confirm if your mobile data is turned on and if you are able to browse the internet using your cellular connection (not Wi-Fi)? If you are unsure, let me know and I can guide you on how to check this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for confirming that mobile data is enabled and you have a strong 5G signal. The next step is to check if your phone's APN settings are correct, as incorrect APN settings can prevent MMS from working. Please check your APN settings and let me know if the MMSC URL is set. If you need instructions on how to check this, let me know your phone's make and model."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for providing your APN settings. The APN name and MMSC URL appear to be set, which is good. Next, let's check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled, as it can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please check if Wi-Fi Calling is turned on. If it is, please turn it off and then try sending an MMS again. Let me know the result."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Since Wi-Fi Calling is off and your APN settings look correct, let's try resetting your APN settings to default, as there may still be a configuration issue. After resetting, you will need to reboot your device for the changes to take effect. Please reset your APN settings to default, then restart your phone. Once your phone is back on, try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying those steps. Since the issue persists, let's check if your data plan limit has been reached, as this can prevent MMS from working. I will check your data usage for your line now."
}

{
  "message": "It appears that you have used 15.1GB of data this billing cycle, which is over your plan's 15GB data limit. This can prevent MMS from working, as MMS requires mobile data. You can add more data (up to 2GB) to your line for $2.00 per GB. Would you like to refuel your data now so you can resume sending MMS messages?"
}

{
  "message": "2GB of data has been successfully added to your line for $4.00. Please try sending an MMS message again. If it still does not work, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. Since you have available data and all basic settings appear correct, the next step is to check if your line has international roaming enabled. Sometimes, if you are outside your home network and roaming is not enabled, MMS may not work. I will check and enable roaming for your line if needed."
}

{
  "message": "Roaming has now been enabled on your line. Please try sending an MMS message again. If you are traveling or outside your usual coverage area, this should help. Let me know if you are still unable to send MMS messages after this step."
}

{
  "message": "I'm glad to hear that your MMS messages are working now! If you have any other questions or need further assistance in the future, feel free to reach out. Have a great day!"
